{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A prayer of the afflicted</b> — Some say: this prayer was composed by a maskil who has fallen into the hands of his enemies. The correct view is that it follows the prophetic mode, spoken in the voice of the people of the exile. The proof: 'for YHWH has built Zion' (v. 17), and also 'this shall be written for a later generation' (v. 19)." "<b>And the word</b> יעטוף — like: העטופים ברעב (those wrapped in hunger, Lamentations 4:9)." "<b>And the meaning of</b> ישפוך — that he pours out all that is in his heart."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:42.658600569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}